# Mosquitto ACL — PRODUCTION
#
# Enforces topic isolation via the %c (client_id) pattern so even if the
# shared device password leaks, a compromised client can only publish to
# its own namespace. Every ESP32 MUST connect with client_id = device_id.
#
# Authenticated clients by default have NO access. Rules below grant:
#   - Any client: publish telemetry + status to sleeppad/{own}/{sec,min,status}
#   - Any client: read + write sleeppad/{own}/cmd  (subscribe to factory_reset
#                 + clear the retained command after handling it)
#   - Backend subscriber: read all sleeppad/# + write to sleeppad/+/cmd so it
#                 can publish remote commands like factory_reset.

# --- Devices (applies to every authenticated client via pattern) ---
pattern write sleeppad/%c/sec
pattern write sleeppad/%c/min
pattern write sleeppad/%c/status
pattern read  sleeppad/%c/cmd
pattern write sleeppad/%c/cmd

# --- Backend subscriber (single user used for both subscribe + cmd publish) ---
user sleeppad-subscriber
topic read  sleeppad/#
topic write sleeppad/+/cmd
